// PARAM: --analysis parity
// The boundary of what Parity can say, kept as an explicit witness so the
// PROVED cases next door are not mistaken for general-purpose precision.
// x is Even here and the concrete value is genuinely fixed (4), but the
// parity lattice has exactly four elements -- Bot, Even, Odd, Top -- and
// carries no magnitude information whatsoever, so "x is Even" is the most
// it can conclude and x == 4 stays UNKNOWN.
// The concrete mechanism: parity_classify_check decides an equality only
// when the two sides' parities are disjoint (Even vs Odd), which refutes;
// it can never confirm one, since equal parity is necessary but nowhere
// near sufficient for equal values. --analysis interval proves this same
// check outright.
void main() {
  x := 2 + 2;
  __voblint_check(x == 4) // UNKNOWN
}
